<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.draft.reads ~ the drafts a standoff brought inside

`drafts <uri>` names the drafts the carrier's standoffs loaded into the worn face's draft layer, by title, so a person sees what `keep-both` would keep. `lares get` reads each draft. The verb writes nothing and asks no confirmation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ which-drafts

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`which-drafts` params=`uri/lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/example ~ list the drafts the standoff loaded`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ uri

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`uri` params=`takes/lar-address needs/required seat/1 as/<uri> ~ the carrier whose standoff drafts to name`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ read

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`read` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ a read of the worn face's draft layer; it writes nothing`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[carriage.draft.reads uri/<uri>]] ~ drafts names a carrier`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

